Infected port: vglReserveCompressedMips. With it on, level 0 of a compressed texture (glCompressedTexImage2D) is
allocated with room for the whole mip chain, and a later level that fits is written in place. Each level is swizzled
by an asynchronous sceGxmTransferCopy; a level that needed a bigger buffer used to vgl_realloc it while the GPU could
still be writing an earlier level into the old one, so the caller had to sceGxmTransferFinish between levels, and that
wait (for whatever the GPU was doing) cost 10 to 15 ms an HD texture on the console. The realloc that remains (the
hint off, or a chain larger than reserved) now waits for the transfers itself. Off by default.

--- a/source/vitaGL.h
+++ b/source/vitaGL.h
@@ -1161,6 +1161,12 @@
 // that the previous custom-shader draw already set and nothing has changed since (off by default).
 void vglSkipRedundantState(GLboolean enable);
 
+// Infected port (patch 0004): level 0 of a compressed texture (glCompressedTexImage2D) reserves room for its whole mip
+// chain, so that uploading the other levels never reallocates the buffer while the GPU still swizzles a level into it,
+// and nobody has to wait for the GPU between levels (sceGxmTransferFinish). Costs a third more memory for a compressed
+// texture that never gets its levels. Off by default.
+void vglReserveCompressedMips(GLboolean enable);
+
 // calloc implementation for vitaGL internal memory pools.
 void *vglCalloc(uint32_t nmember, uint32_t size);
 
